<spell-notebook "calendar theming">
	<header level="1">
		Calendar
		<header>A calendar lets a user pick a date, a time, or both.</>
	</>
	<calendar-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-calendar-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` for every
			calendar), or on the box through `::part(calendar)` or `::part(popup)`. Style the pieces with `::part()`:
			`input` and `control` (the field), `trigger` (the icon button), `popup`, `header` with `previous`, `title` and
			`next`, `grid`, `cell` and `today`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-calendar {
			  --ui-calendar-cell-padding: 0.75em;
			}
			ui-calendar::part(cell) {
			  border-radius: 50%;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`color` remaps the shared `--ui-color`, so a theme's hues work here too. Never set the `--_ui-calendar-*`
				names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-calendar" playground>
				<ui-calendar value="2026-09-30T14:30" locale="en-US" placeholder="Date and time" today></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
